#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229142 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5bc609b-dc5b-52e9-9f0e-206f32bb829b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Homogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "280d8127-c31a-5e2e-b9dc-665b3585f060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-9t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555084} {:answer/id #uuid "44c32af4-4f13-53b5-8974-40ae755cae35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{9t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555147} {:answer/id #uuid "48431481-3e8e-57a8-83d2-eb0cb39cf23b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555154} {:answer/id #uuid "a2c5ce55-c333-5011-848b-c5650ca56801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555391} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a1cb7e-8b62-5bfd-ab90-3eb838df358f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-9t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2c5ce55-c333-5011-848b-c5650ca56801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555391} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cd5bc44-1d8a-5b80-a78e-d0c95223991b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "021e3fe3-3d72-56fe-ac1a-be1f9dae2590" :question/math-academy-id "q-335026" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=9y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=9x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555774 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229143 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c48896b-a018-521e-946b-fe65b686effd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -5\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555247} {:answer/id #uuid "7a745ab5-2e30-5358-a661-1005ce9fee4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555285} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5a344b-c228-5070-a3de-d96f53cbd405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555331} {:answer/id #uuid "cf972ef6-5de2-58b9-b5d8-6de313e595af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555494} {:answer/id #uuid "da11d876-2fe9-5885-b371-78fffbd4906e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e5a344b-c228-5070-a3de-d96f53cbd405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555331} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9bfc61d-9208-5f2a-9171-0d8c90db3cd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "27a5f814-886e-5a61-acf9-facf209e99cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-335263" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555867 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229144 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential: Shifted Initial Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d2dabb0-502b-562b-b584-741bd2219b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin(3(t-2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d2dabb0-502b-562b-b584-741bd2219b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin(3(t-2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555287} :answer-field/id #uuid "12370503-03e0-554e-be1b-d6e2ad47764c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555648} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d71b20dd-cdf6-5315-9b31-8b02be6facce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos(3(t-2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d71b20dd-cdf6-5315-9b31-8b02be6facce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos(3(t-2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555515} :answer-field/id #uuid "645a6766-29a4-5adf-89b5-f8cdeb82aee5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ea042103-925d-51d6-8c12-93baa97ad8a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-335432" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(2) \\\\ y(2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"130px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-2)}\\,x(2) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3(t-2)) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3(t-2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3(t-2)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3(t-2))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3(t-2))\\, \\\\ \\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3(t-2))\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229144 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential: Shifted Initial Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3c3294a-f087-5672-a53e-117506420382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391581} {:answer/id #uuid "601ea9e6-24b0-535e-bb17-49ca178db97e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391582} {:answer/id #uuid "59b758f5-6067-571d-908b-9e50262c9da7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391583} {:answer/id #uuid "66384a82-a5a2-5020-8b9b-8db002bae474" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391584} {:answer/id #uuid "70ed0219-7267-5410-9f26-31afb335cb12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66384a82-a5a2-5020-8b9b-8db002bae474" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391584} :answer-field/id #uuid "afd92e9b-c3b2-5f27-ae61-1167e9f32949" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ab60b60-d1a6-5ef2-aaf8-6579001f22b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-335448" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-4x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(1) \\\\ y(1)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1)) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229145 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c" :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution: Homogeneous Systems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "614d6ab5-5628-5fbe-818a-c13fdda2c28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396938} {:answer/id #uuid "ce094f55-879b-5b96-bedb-c8a97168bac2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396939} {:answer/id #uuid "cccff4fe-20c3-5cb7-9681-92cc25121511" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396940} {:answer/id #uuid "ab84e7ed-d6a8-520d-8b8d-917218916f48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce094f55-879b-5b96-bedb-c8a97168bac2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396939} :answer-field/id #uuid "62e5d724-e4aa-50ec-8d98-2ca352e011f4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396937} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3461c8f3-6347-5cda-a1c7-cd2ab24c6c21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396943} {:answer/id #uuid "41161c5d-5b28-5637-adb6-191d50f983ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396944} {:answer/id #uuid "411ea3ea-3c55-50ae-abd5-5130b8a1d446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396945} {:answer/id #uuid "a18ae187-4ca1-50ee-ba3f-d6af9219c439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating the equation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41161c5d-5b28-5637-adb6-191d50f983ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396944} :answer-field/id #uuid "d10c4b52-29cf-597a-97d0-5df761b842ca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396942} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5363f0a4-bc32-5773-a19c-82bd214aee7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396948} {:answer/id #uuid "83b75a12-331a-52aa-8a26-b868726772a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396949} {:answer/id #uuid "9f3f9f52-0d94-5534-85e6-03b3ff052905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "using diagonalization of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396950} {:answer/id #uuid "c4e0fc6c-fed0-5c5b-bab5-4daeb2418d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating the equation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5363f0a4-bc32-5773-a19c-82bd214aee7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396948} :answer-field/id #uuid "b441f599-459e-58bd-b0d0-12769ed6a804" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b476f440-04ac-55c0-bbfe-8012f8f71f27" :question/math-academy-id "q-336477" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$  \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by  {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by substitution from lines {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from $\\text{L2},$ we have the identity\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c.\n$$\n\nEvaluating this identity at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L3}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{evaluating both sides at }t=0.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L4},$ and $\\text{L5}.$ From $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nand from $\\text{L4}$ we know ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={I}_{n}c=c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L5}.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by $\\text{substituting }{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}\\text{ into }x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$, $\\text{L2},$ $\\text{L5},$ and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L1}$ we have ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At},$ and from $\\text{L5}$ we know $c=x(0).$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ from $\\text{L1}$ and $c=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$ into $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ (line $\\text{L2}$), we obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and substitution from $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L5}.$"}]}
